======================================================================
PROJECT NOTICE
==============

The Agentic Framework project is released under the Apache License 2.0.

This project represents the author's research, architectural design,
methodology, orchestration patterns, workflow structures, execution
strategies, and software engineering practices for building reliable,
agentic AI systems.

The author believes that the primary value of this project resides in
its architectural concepts, system design decisions, execution
methodologies, orchestration patterns, reliability mechanisms,
workflow structures, and operational practices.

Examples include but are not limited to:

* Multi-stage agent orchestration
* Self-briefing workflows
* Self-correction and introspection loops
* Capability-driven execution planning
* Tool routing and execution strategies
* Autonomous workflow execution patterns
* Reliability and guardrail architectures
* Structured planning methodologies
* Retrospection and reflection mechanisms
* Local-model optimization patterns
* Hybrid deterministic and LLM-driven execution systems
* Agent observability and monitoring patterns
* Execution recovery and failure handling mechanisms
* Agent workflow coordination techniques
* Prompt layering and execution control systems

Publication of this repository serves as public disclosure of these
concepts and their implementation as of the publication date.

Nothing in this notice modifies, restricts, supersedes, or limits
the permissions granted by the Apache License 2.0.

